course: dictionary
lesson: 9630
title: Student and its many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A student is a person who learns, usually at a school, college or university. The word can also mean someone who studies a subject carefully, at any age. The clues in a sentence show you which meaning fits.
explain: «Some zoos let apes play memory games on touch screens, and in a famous test young chimps remembered flashing numbers faster than university students.» The word university tells you the students are learners at a university, not at a primary school.
explain: Places can change a word too. In the UK, younger children at school are often called pupils, but in the USA student is used for all ages. «Struggling learner» means a weak student, so the context here is a school learner.
fact: A student is a person who learns at a school, college or university.
fact: A student of something is a person who studies it carefully, at any age.
fact: «Students» is the plural form, so one student becomes many students.
fact: In the UK, younger children at school are often called pupils, while in the USA student is used for all ages.
fact: Phrases such as «student council» and «exchange student» use student to mean a person who is part of a school or learning group.
exercise: «Some zoos let apes play memory games, and in a famous test young chimps beat university students.» Who are the university students? | Young chimps | *People who learn at a university | Animals that live in zoos | Teachers at a primary school
exercise: «Struggling learner» means a weak student. In this sentence, what is a student? | A machine that makes a noise | A shop that sells books | A kind of test for chimps | *A learner, a person who is learning
exercise: In the UK, what are younger children at school often called? | Warlords | Students only | Advertisers | *Pupils
test: A student of music is a person who... | Teaches music to adults only | *Studies music carefully, at any age | Sells music in a shop | Plays the drums in a band
test: Which word means a learner at a school, college or university? | Senior | *Student | Treaty | Warlord
exam: Read this: «Advertisers like soft words: mature students sounds nicer than old students.» Why would an advert say mature students? | *Because it sounds softer and nicer | Because mature means small | Because it means the students are angry | Because old students are never learners
